Gap 1 (radiation‑resilient encoding) underlies all five at the physical layer.

1.4 The Agency Problem and the Trilemma

The companion document requires knowledge infrastructure to be queryable by AI agents, legible to humans, and fault‑tolerant against decades‑scale hardware degradation. This triad engenders the Memory Legibility Trilemma (conjectured in §2.4): no single representation simultaneously maximises machine‑queryability, human legibility, and bounded fault‑tolerance overhead for high‑entropy domains.

