Chapter 7 – Integrated Architecture and Co‑Design

The duality functor \Phi not only proves mathematical identity but enables co‑design: an algorithm for optimal battery charging can be compiled into an optimal memory verification schedule. The Lyapunov stability theorem ensures that energy‑driven pruning is safe. The CRDT merge theorem guarantees that knowledge drift is bounded and recoverable.

Proposition 7.1 (Pareto Frontier). The joint energy–memory optimal trade‑off satisfies

\frac{e_{\min}}{e_0} + \frac{m_{\min}}{m_0} \ge 1 - \frac{\beta}{2},

with \beta encoding the coupling. The frontier is convex; co‑design pushes it outward.

Future integrated testbed: Couple a simulated lunar microgrid (PV, battery, RFC) with the CRDT knowledge store. Stress‑test under simultaneous energy and communication blackouts to quantify the joint resilience surface.

