Appendix F. Derivation of the Minimum Viable Context Population (Theorem 6.5)

Theorem 6.5.
Assume the civilisational memory (Layer 6) decays at a rate that depends on the number of living context‑holders P(t) as

\lambda_6(P) = \lambda_{6,0}\,\frac{P_{\text{ref}}}{P(t)},
\tag{F.1}

with constant \lambda_{6,0} and reference population P_{\text{ref}}. The regeneration rate v_6 is bounded by a maximal feasible effort v_6^{\max}. The steady‑state fidelity is

F_6^* = \frac{v_6}{\lambda_6(P)+v_6},
\qquad
\mathrm{MRI}_6 = \frac{v_6}{\lambda_6(P)}.
\tag{F.2}

Let P^* be the population below which \mathrm{MRI}_6 < 1 even under maximal regeneration, i.e. the condition for steady‑state fidelity to stay above 0.5. Then

P^* = \frac{\lambda_{6,0}\,P_{\text{ref}}}{v_6^{\max}}.
\tag{F.3}

Proof.
Set v_6 = v_6^{\max} and require \mathrm{MRI}_6 \ge 1:

\frac{v_6^{\max}}{\lambda_6(P)} \ge 1 \;\Longrightarrow\; \lambda_6(P) \le v_6^{\max}.

Substituting (F.1) gives

\lambda_{6,0}\frac{P_{\text{ref}}}{P} \le v_6^{\max}
\;\Longrightarrow\; P \ge \frac{\lambda_{6,0}P_{\text{ref}}}{v_6^{\max}}.

Therefore the minimal population that just meets the condition is exactly P^* as stated. For any P<P^* we have \mathrm{MRI}_6<1 and consequently F_6^*<0.5. ∎

